def transfer(frm, to, amnt):
    """ attempts to transfers "amnt" money from "frm" to "to" """
    
    # total balance of all "frm" accounts is not less than "amnt"
    
    total_balance = sum([acnt.money for acnt in frm.accounts])
    assert total_balance >= amnt

    for acnt in frm.accounts:
        if acnt.money >= amnt:
            acnt.money -= amnt
            to.accounts[0].money += amnt
            return True

    return False
```

This assertion is checking that the total balance of all accounts associated with the "frm" person is not less than "amnt", else it will raise an AssertionError. In other words, it makes sure that enough money is available to perform the transfer. If the assert statement is true, then the transfer is carried out. If it is false, then the transfer fails.
